ir3: a prefetched fragment sample takes the sampler's own index

GL binds a texture and its sampler at one index, so ir3 used the texture index
for both. Metal does not: QuartzCore's shaders sample, for example, texture 3
with sampler 0, and the prefetched sample then read sampler 3. Same fix as
HackiOS components/metal/tools/mesa26/darwin.patch (ir3_compiler_nir.c).

diff --git a/src/freedreno/ir3/ir3_compiler_nir.c b/src/freedreno/ir3/ir3_compiler_nir.c
--- a/src/freedreno/ir3/ir3_compiler_nir.c
+++ b/src/freedreno/ir3/ir3_compiler_nir.c
@@ -3605,7 +3605,7 @@
          sampler = ir3_COV(b, sampler, TYPE_U32, TYPE_U16);
       } else {
          sampler = create_immed_typed(b, tex->sampler_index, TYPE_U16);
-         info.samp_idx = tex->texture_index;
+         info.samp_idx = tex->sampler_index;
       }

       info.samp_tex = ir3_collect(b, texture, sampler);
